Who are we?
The Park Foundation takes care of the Park, located on the Nieuwe Maas at the foot of the Euromast. The Park is Rotterdam's largest green national monument and a popular place for 1.6 million visitors a year. It was designed in 1852 in English landscape style by landscape architects Zocher. The Parkteam is committed to connecting visitors to nature, art & culture and each other every day. The team consists of gardeners for the specialist green maintenance, reception staff of the Parkpaviljoen, the meeting room for park visitors, and the colleagues of the office who provide the organisation, programming and communication.
Who are we looking for?
You have a warm heart for nature and culture. We expect you to have thorough knowledge of the management and maintenance of green heritage, or from experience or training you can effectively acquire it. You are a people manager who manages to connect and inspire the employees of the Park and a management and organizational talent, which puts its hands out of the sleeves and (sometimes) literally stands in the mud. You can preferably start autumn 2026, by January 1st 2027 as our new director.
What are you gonna do?
You are in charge of a team of approx. 10 employees and you are responsible for efficient business operations. In consultation with the board of the Foundation het Park you will draw up the strategic policy plan and the annual plans and report on the progress. You will help position the Park as an attractive free accessible, green and high-quality location for a wide audience.
As a strong sparring partner of the stakeholders of the Park, such as the municipality of Rotterdam, Stichting Droom en Daad, (green) contractors, experts and advisors, you stand up for your own vision within established policy frameworks. Based on the primary objective of maintaining, managing and making it liveable for all Rotterdammers and visitors of the city, you will initiate the Park programme. As a member of the team and sparring partner of the board, you are one of the ambassadors of the Park. In the coming years, developing the community of stakeholders and friends of the Park will receive a lot of attention.
What do we ask of you?
• You have knowledge of, and insight into, historical green management, or you are able to acquire it effectively;
• You are a strategist who also wants to join the team as a colleague, both at the office, in the Parkpavilion, and in the green;
• You are a .people manager with demonstrable experience in managing a small to medium-sized organisation;
• You have affinity with the combination of nature, culture and recreation;
• You are able to develop a vision of stakeholder management for further positioning and strengthening of the Park;
• You are able to conduct the organisation's operations, supported where necessary by external consultants and service providers;
• You work smoothly with IT and software for this function: Word, Excel, Powerpoint, Afas, etc;
• You are Dutch and speak English;
• You have no difficulty working outside regular times.
What do we offer?
• A salary between € 5000,- and € 6,000 gross per month based on a 40-hour working week;
• 8% holiday allowance, 25 days' holidays based on full-time employment, participation in our pension provision and travel expenses of € 0.23 per kilometre;
• The most beautiful workplace in Rotterdam: in the Park Pavilion;
• The possibility of flexible working days and part work at home;
• Last but not least: You will become part of a team of fellow fellow citizens who work with love on and in Rotterdam's largest green national monument.
