Are you that dare-doer who is helping us advance the energy transition? Do you get energy from ensuring safety and health, working practice-oriented and dare to engage in conversation when needed? Then we're looking for you!
As HSE Advisor at Ennatural, you work daily on a safe and healthy working environment within our projects, heat networks and installations throughout the Netherlands. You are present on site and are visible in improving and ensuring safe and healthy working, both in new projects and in existing locations. You are the first contact point for managers, managers, installation managers and OIV managers in the field of Health, Safety & Environment (HSE). You're close to practice, you know what's going on in the field and you dare to intervene when safety is under pressure.
Your role is highly practice- and field-oriented. In case of incident reports, you go in and take your interviews. In addition, you conduct inspections and RI&Es and ensure clear interpretation and feedback. You are not ultimately responsible for HSE, but play a crucial role in analysing, signaling and advising. To achieve this:
Guide and analyse your incident and accident reports (e.g. through the Safe Working App), including partners' employees;
Monitor compliance with security procedures on site;
Give your toolboxes and instructions on topics such as working at height, asbestos and working in contaminated soil;
If necessary, you can agree with supervisors such as the Labour Inspectorate and the State surveillance of the Mines in the case of geothermal heat;
Contribute to developing and applying procedures, instructions and the HSE Manual;
You work closely with the HSE Specialist (policy-based), the Crisis & HSE Manager and other stakeholders, with your practical experience providing direct input for further professionalisation of safety within Ennatural.
What we ask
A practical HSE Adviser with a completed MBO or HBO course, preferably towards Integrated Safety, Safety Science (MVK/MBO4), Environmental Science, KAM or a similar training programme, which will strengthen our team for 32 January 2004 per week. Further:
Can you work effectively both independently and in a team;
You stand firmly in your shoes and dare to engage in the conversation about safety;
Are you communicative strong, both orally and in writing in Dutch, and can clearly transfer safety information to colleagues and partners.
What we offer
Sustainable relationships can help you build a sustainable future together. We're happy to give you what you deserve.
Fine secondary employment conditions such as an NS Business Card, smartphone, laptop and car of the business;
Space to work hybrid including a fully ergonomic homework site;
The function falls into salary scale 5 of our job home and has a salary range of €4.187 to €6.094 gross per month;
