As Senior Teeling Specialist, you play an important role in achieving optimal crop performance and high-quality seed production. You are responsible for the cultivation of one or more crops and are continuously working on improving growing conditions, production processes and cultivation results. In doing so, you work closely with production specialists, growers and researchers to determine, evaluate and further develop crop targets. From your expertise, you have a direct influence on the quality, yield and future resistance of our conventional and organic crops at the Wervershoof site.
In this role you will be involved with:
Managing, coaching and developing a team or functionally guiding a less experienced Agronomy;
To bear the final responsibility for the cultivation of one or more crops, including climate control, plant protection, fertilization and irrigation;
Optimising cultivation processes within the set cultivation objectives and budgets;
Analyzing crop results and translating insights into practical improvements;
Working with growers and researchers to define, monitor and evaluate crop targets;
Promoting and monitoring a healthy, safe and sustainable working environment.
What you bring as a future colleague
As a Senior Teelt specialist, you bring a strong combination of professional knowledge, ownership and coaching skills. You know how to optimize cultivation results and can make informed choices based on data, observations and experience. In addition, you can easily work with different stakeholders and guide and motivate your fellow officers to achieve common goals. Thanks to your planned approach, you keep an overview, set your priorities and adjust in time where necessary.
You also have:
A MBO or HBO diploma in a relevant direction, such as Gardening, Agronomy or Plant Sciences;
Minimum 5 years of relevant work experience within successful crops and/or seed production;
Experience with climate computers and optimisation of cultivation conditions;
Good control of the Dutch and English language, both orally and in writing;
Strong analytical skills and the ability to translate cultivation data into improvement actions;
Experience in managing, guiding or coaching colleagues within a growing environment.
enza Seeds as your employer
